 "cell_semantics": "fails = outputs on which garak's detector fired (garak calls this attack success); total_evaluated = prompts x generations; counts verbatim from garak eval entries",
 "method_limitations": [
  "garak detectors are heuristic string/regex/parse rules; a hit means the rule matched, not that the model is unsafe",
  "a hit rate is not a safety grade and no ranking between the two models is claimed",
  "small generations: 3 per prompt, and the fixed seed reaches Ollama, so many attempts returned 3 identical outputs (see identical_generations_per_probe); the effective sample is nearer the prompt count than the output count",
  "20 prompts per probe sampled by garak from pools of up to 256 (seeded; both models received byte-identical prompts); ansiescape.AnsiRaw ran all 58",
  "mitigation.MitigationBypass is inverted: an answer without a refusal phrase counts as a bypass even if it is harmless",
  "encoding 0 hits may reflect a small model's inability to decode, not resistance",
  "two quantised (Q4_K_M) models on one GPU, one run each; no replication yet"
 ],
